    "body": "Implementations should defer to the operation system as much as possible to avoid this scenario. That said on some platforms the Chromium implementation does have to parse descriptors itself. This danger should be called out in the specification but I'm unsure of anything more we could say normatively.\n\nIn the example you give the real `bNumEndpoints` value isn't exposed to script except by `endpoints.length` on a `USBAlterantiveInterface` instance. This forces an implementation to either refuse to enumerate the device entirely or just ignore the mismatch, returning the lesser of `bNumEndpoints` and the true value.",
